Z||000000||Seanh||04-17-2001||10:48 PM||||My parents are in love with Lincoln Towncars (they have 4 now). They just bought an 88 Signiture Towncar for a good deal, we know why now! The engine developed a nasty know after overheating once. A mechanic told us the engine probally had the knock long before it overheated on us, due to previous overheating. Long story short, the engine should be rebuilt. It has a 5.0 302 with EFI right now. We are debating what to do. Rebuilt this engine, get a junk yard engine, put in a newer engine? We are leaning tword the newer engine part. Lincoln started putting a 4.6L Overhead cam engine in the cars after 91 I think, cuz our 94 and 96 both have it. Anyway, would the 4.6L bolt right up to the tranny and cradle? I would think so, since I'm pretty sure its the same block right? Alls I would need is the computer and wireing harness for the new engine right? Any ideas please let me know. Thanks!||||reg||1
