Z||000005||beer_stud_21||04-18-2001||03:52 PM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.coolcats.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.coolcats.net</A>   it is a site dedicated to Fox bodied T-birds and Cougars 83-88 About half of them have the 302 V8 and some guys there have upgraded to HO and even swapped for the Cobra spec 5.0  At the bottom of the main page there is a link to a small forum.  There isnt a lot of action there because the user base is really small but the guys are really nice and will be happy to answer your questions.  There are also a few lincon owners.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||04-18-2001||09:12 PM||||I found an 88 5.0 for $560.00 and a 4.6L Cobra HO racing engine for around $1000. It currently has the 5.0, but honestly I don't, IMO, think it has as much power as the new DOHC 4.6 in the newer car. How should I got about rebuilding this engine if I do so decided to do that? Should I buy the $1K rebuild kit, or buy the parts seperatly and salvage what I can from the old engine? I think it would cost just about the same to rebuild the engine as it would to put in a fairly new DOHC 4.6L engine. This isn't my car, and my parents aren't lookin for speed and power, just fairly good gas milage and a quite engine like the newer Lincolns. I will check out that site also. Thanks. (Iv kicked the crap outta Mustangs and Camaro's left and right with the 96 4.6L TownCar. If you floor it off the line it will bark the tires off the line and shifting into 2nd. I love luxary cars that can perform.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||04-19-2001||01:28 PM||||One thing that I have found working with GM and Ford vehicles' wiring is that GM is very consistant with the wiring color and purpose between all of its vehicles. I really realized this when I put a Grand Prix 727 ecm in my Fiero and all the wiring colors for everything matched up, with only a few "extras", but on the fords that I have worked on, they change stuff from year to year and model to model. You would have fun wiring a different engine up to it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Seanh||04-19-2001||07:15 PM||||I went out to the local yard today and found a 92 4.6L Lincoln Engine with 81K on it for $975. If it will be a direct bolt on with little or no modification we are going to buy it. I am going to talk to Ford tomarrow to see if it will bolt up right or what will have to be changed. Hope this works, can't wait to try it. This engine comes with a wiring harness, and I'll have to buy the computer seperatly. I work with wireing everday, so this shouldn't be to much more complicated then installing Remote car starters and alarms. Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spektyr||04-20-2001||02:17 AM||||On a similar note, does anyone know what cars I can use to find suspension upgrades for my 89 Town Car?<P>I realize it won't ever act like a tricked out Mustang, but I'd like to correct the massive body roll and generally make it handle 'right' instead of plowing through a turn if I decide to push it a bit.<P>I'm thinking front and rear anti-sway bars, and maybe dropping the upper A-arm if it isn't already set close to parallel to the lower A-arm.  (haven't checked it yet to see)<P>Any other upgrade ideas or ideas where to find the parts?<P>I'm thinking the T-bird parts might be compatible, but I'd like to find out if anyone knows for sure.||||reg||1
