Z||000011||rogergarrison||04-21-2001||08:09 AM||||about the only things that are same as tbird is the Mark series. TC's interchange with Mercury Gran Marquis and Ford LTD. Lot of suspension component on TC is Ford full size van, pickup. So you could try that. I know a guy that put his 4wd pickup stuff in his Mark IV, called it 'MARK 4X4'.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||04-21-2001||06:51 PM||||In a related idea- back when we were painting Limo's for a local escourt service, one of them blew the engine and it was replaced with a 302 HO from a Mustang. That thing would really haul! We all loved to drive that one.||||reg||1
Z||000013||2birds||04-22-2001||11:41 PM||||Ditto what rogergarrison said.  The town car has a frame, unlike the Fox-chassied 83-88 T-bird/Cougar twins, the 79-93 Mustang/Cougar, the 83-86 LTD II's, and the Mark 7's.  <BR>I own a 94 Mustang GT (5.0) and a 97 T-bird (4.6).  The 4.6 and 5.0 might as well be made by two different companies.  They are completely different.  The only thing they have in common is the level of difficulty to access the oil filter without spilling the contents.<BR>Stick with a 5.0.  They are plentiful, and it will bolt right in, and parts are way cheaper, compared to the 4.6.  <BR>Of course, a 460 will fit easier than a 4.6, also... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||Seanh||04-22-2001||11:46 PM||||I looked into the 460 and a 400, but all the ones the junk yard had are carbed. I want fuel injected all the way. I did figure out that the 4.6L will not bolt to my tranny, but I am looking into a 4.6 compatable tranny if I could get it cheap. I might just buy another 5.0 and rebuild it in the grage, then drop it in and sell or part out the old one. Know any cheap way to Fuel inject a 400 or 460?||||reg||1
